# cp.async with a register src-size, 16 on lanes 0..15 and 0 on the
# others: ptxas writes LDGSTS with an ignore-src predicate. The register
# is not read, so which lanes read, and how much, is not known: the row,
# the per-execution read and the totals are bounds.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/cp_async_src_size.ptx --ncu %fixtures/micro/cp_async_src_size.ncu.json | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/cp_async_src_size.ptx --ncu %fixtures/micro/cp_async_src_size.ncu.json | FileCheck "%s"
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_cp_async_src_size( // grid 1×1×1 | block 64×1×1 | shared memory 1,024 B/CTA | per launch: global load <= 1,024 B; shared store 1,024 B; param load 512 B{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	cp.async.cg.shared.global 	[%r4], [%rd3], 16, %r5; // shared store [16·%tid.x + buf] wavefronts/req ? (wavefronts not modelled) | global load [16·%tid.x + param_0] sectors/req <= 17 (ideal 16){{$}}
CHECK: global load <= 16 B (predicated)  warp: <= 17 sectors (ideal <= 16)
CHECK: per thread per execution: global load <= 16 B; shared store 16 B
CHECK: totals per CTA [static]:
CHECK: AI(global) >= 0 flop/B
